VALUES ('b81c7534-1f6c-4788-9c2b-8901e0b9103f', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'The countries of Eastern Europe were known as History Grade 10 Student Textbook "European People''s Democracies" or Soviet satellite states. They were under heavy political, economic and military influence or control of Soviet Russia. The political, military, and ideological barrier erected by the Soviet Union after World War II to seal off itself and its satellite states from open contact with the West and other noncommunist areas was known as Iron Curtain. The term was coined by Winston Churchill in 1946 during his speech in Fulton, Missouri. It was an imaginary political boundary dividing Europe into two separate areas from the end of World War II in 1945 until the end of the Cold War in 1991.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[-0.0009887086,0.024321092,-0.028772607,-0.042280298,0.003580243,-0.03826434,0.047939274,-0.010378519,-0.029232744,-0.09836686,-0.04824676,-0.011787418,0.021840768,0.027541159,0.0017110773,-0.05012835,0.009362997,-0.01044931,0.005468391,0.01822508,-0.009915049,-0.007598313,0.026079044,-0.01609502,0.029190835,0.016081717,-0.014775103,-0.029301709,-0.031531613,0.19052382,0.00016928128,-0.04162139,-0.02755301,0.016844053,-0.029783867,0.007248633,-0.029691521,-0.005615762,0.017444637,0.057845544,0.016979424,-0.027927566,0.01116955,-0.011165481,-0.01012357,-0.029923078,-0.02114295,0.032877035,0.02239086,-0.009303634,-0.01659056,0.03666866,0.007120899,-0.04576459,0.06311441,0.037692927,-0.028218996,-0.032163657,-0.0008486566,-0.0029253536,-0.035368863,0.05521357,-0.007303434,0.031634226,-0.0104821,-0.034774695,0.02669543,-0.067794114,0.013996207,-0.001653744,0.028286217,0.003841585,0.037091564,-0.008968463,-0.060351938,0.0031122111,-0.008561949,-0.017458403,0.04586064,0.020537922,-0.007870642,0.009015318,-0.007826692,0.011380395,0.024336778,0.0014925236,-0.028191028,0.013155735,-0.018323766,-0.007585796,-0.024592973,-0.00082793017,