VALUES ('6f5142ec-c621-4508-ba6f-407d2e9c94c1', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'presented the case of Palestine to the United Nations. The United Nations General Assembly decided the partition of Palestine into Jewish and Arab states. Jerusalem was to be internationalized. The Arabs opposed the decision claiming Palestine only for the Arabs. The Jews partially accepted the plan and proclaimed the establishment of the state of Israel on May 14, 1948. The First Arab-Israeli War of 1948 On May 15, 1948, the governments of Egypt, Syria, Iraq, and Trans-Jordan (Jordan) declared war on Israel. The Jewish successfully repulsed repeated Arab attacks. By early 1949 the Israelis had managed to occupy half of Jerusalem and the northwest coastal area along the Mediterranean Sea. In Israel, the war is remembered as the War of Independence. In the Arab world, it came to be known as the Nakbah (or Nakba; “Catastrophe”) because of the large number of refugees and displaced persons resulting from the war.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[-0.019653777,0.03650111,-0.0038371612,-0.039950624,0.013963346,-0.018644413,-0.02166514,0.004699807,0.0034661687,-0.113047846,-0.04113581,0.029278914,0.02345451,0.0022491168,-0.010648467,-0.045852344,0.027974587,0.0037195939,-0.008247763,0.008007939,0.040052965,-0.018176379,0.016818417,0.0032209505,-0.024777543,0.010532328,0.023252754,-0.026639873,-0.005017545,0.1765273,-0.028303895,-0.010581066,-0.029374847,0.019807478,-0.016102716,0.023034558,-0.027862383,-0.025559008,-0.009014812,0.01295123,0.027524672,0.0000693531,0.019670911,0.04843158,0.0005377186,-0.04930304,-0.046828516,0.04299354,0.020986086,0.022613283,0.028587569,0.008292623,0.025451249,-0.032379195,0.041979037,0.030615266,-0.0048728418,-0.00023689898,-0.0098870685,0.00084541534,-0.008029947,0.049690776,-0.0062050773,0.029314289,-0.01389083,-0.016413843,-0.02194175,-0.043964524,0.020731393,0.0011656336,0.029599944,-0.008766446,0.046210013,-0.01606889