VALUES ('a20f24e6-363b-43e0-8828-a8b4a6785fb0', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Unit Introduction Unit learning outcomes At the end of this unit, the students will be able to: • elaborate how the British established their dominance in Ethiopia immediately after the termination the Fascist Italian rule; • explain how the United States was involved in consolidating autocracy in Ethiopia; • assess the causes and results of the Ethiopian Revolution of 1974; • compare and contrast the land policies of the Imperial and the Derg regime; • outline the major opposition movements against the imperial regime in Ethiopia; • describe the process of federation and union of Eritrea with Ethiopia; • distinguish the major factors for the decline of the Derg regime.', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[-0.004690462,0.015815029,-0.0056444323,-0.0007572072,0.030022295,0.006654952,-0.008971486,0.013248402,-0.01450364,-0.1157303,-0.056154825,0.008381202,0.04922769,0.012568974,-0.019092202,-0.061709963,-0.0016294135,-0.015307325,0.021521507,-0.010434641,0.029451283,0.0045715505,0.00881507,-0.014207175,-0.012889824,-0.00558184,-0.02424056,-0.028712915,0.0016684132,0.19270307,-0.03109006,-0.07888451,-0.0075886343,0.015497657,-0.008617456,-0.012768134,-0.019096259,0.0043098805,0.023289945,0.0038510736,0.03205795,0.016738316,-0.026534887,-0.003129911,-0.0046778885,-0.025276784,-0.03554776,0.026449855,0.015287634,0.0073266667,-0.0056389426,0.0023712788,0.031857114,-0.06418497,0.017750746,0.04970451,-0.0014327262,0.015843164,0.012289257,0.01332834,0.0013440759,0.030495346,-0.0046720807,0.020609915,-0.014044069,-0.0061535044,0.01626014,-0.042190332,-0.008879689,0.003809919,0.025771204,0.011318048,0.025919339,0.007702618,-0.055804893,0.018893892,0.0018193764,0.0026159172,0.03343976,0.032788258,0.020103432,0.03160617,-0.0260282,0.026061926,0.019025343,-0.0040493063,0.039243005,0.0053298245,0.031489555,-0.014584889,-0.02616478,0.0147211505,0.008412613,-0.07060169,