VALUES ('9b90d4a1-63ed-476e-a124-a8bb532cb9f5', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000400', 'Part I: Multiple choice Items: Choose the best answers from the given alternatives 1. The leading export item of Ethiopia in the post liberation period was A.Gold C. Skin and hides B. Coffee D. Oil seeds and spices 2. By the end of the 1970s the overall industrial base of the country A.played the dominant role as compared to the agricultural sector B. characterized by a primary small scale industry C. was uniformly distributed in all provinces D.was the main source of income 3. From 1942 to 1954 the modern Ethiopian education system was highly influenced A.By the British C. The Church B. By the Americans D. The French 4. The First Five-Year Plan (1957-61) sought to develop a strong infrastructure in transportation and communication aimed A.to get access to mining sector B. to accelerate agricultural development C. to establish regional economic integration with neighboring countries D.to serve the urban population 5. Which of the following countries was not the major Ethiopian partner in imports in the 1960and 70s? A.The USA B. Italy C. Japan D.China Part II: Short Answer 1.Evaluate the administrative and economic reforms introduced during the post-liberation period. History Grade 10 Student Textbook', 'G10-History-STB-2023-web.pdf p.1', '2026.1', 'published', '[0.015319322,0.021200748,0.024951123,-0.056659423,0.025231525,-0.005198173,0.01235261,0.030425156,-0.02090177,-0.11660433,-0.043860007,0.023455236,0.072590016,-0.00974086,-0.07216325,-0.044289548,0.03161312,-0.04022108,0.014296308,0.007758883,0.003608876,0.008984904,0.034834076,0.010550477,-0.03797755,-0.023173628,0.014391853,-0.056971364,0.005603158,0.177909,-0.006361729,-0.025916731,-0.0044908556,-0.014230434,0.0068789143,-0.03066775,-0.0048353663,-0.009309245,-0.00095027505,0.031316075,0.017150829,-0.022538701,-0.016057322,0.009694875,-0.018497074,-0.026371948,-0.03420012,0.030975886,0.011354133,-0.0023710823,0.0136285